  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe current optimization approach uses gradient descent with finite differences, which is computationally expensive and may get stuck in local optima. We propose a more efficient method using exact gradient computation for the maximum overlap, reducing the per-iteration cost and enabling faster convergence. Additionally, multiple initializations and periodic perturbations will help explore the solution space more thoroughly.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nWe seek to minimize C\u2085 = max\u2096 \u222bh(x)(1 - h(x+k)) dx, with h \u2208 [0,1] and \u222bh dx = 1. The overlap integral for each k is calculated as the dot product of h and (1 - h shifted by k). To compute gradients efficiently, for each step, identify the shift k with the maximum overlap and compute gradients only for that k.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na) Initialize h using initial_h_values or a structured waveform.\nb) For each iteration:\n   i) Compute correlation for all shifts k.\n   ii) Identify the shift k_max with maximum overlap.\n   iii) Compute exact gradient for k_max: \u2207C\u2085 = (1 - h_shifted_k_max) for each h[i].\n   iv) Update h using gradient descent, projecting to feasible space.\n   v) Periodically perturb h to escape local minima.\nc) After each update, ensure h remains within [0,1] and sums to n_points / 2.\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Start with initial_h_values and perturb it slightly for multiple optimizations.\n- Use varying learning rates, with adaptive reduction on plateaus.\n- Implementation may test single-perturbation vs. population-based approaches.\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\nThe approach is designed to handle the 600s budget efficiently, with frequent feasibility checks and early termination if time limits are reached. Each iteration is faster due to exact gradients, allowing more iterations or trials.\n\n6. Validation and return contract\nFinal solution must pass feasibility checks (0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1, sum h = 0.5*n_points), and evaluate the objective to ensure C\u2085 \u2264 0.3807.",
